# Test: `directive scheduler=<mode>` REJECTS an unknown mode (E_UnknownDirective).
#
# The valid set is {pool, thread, inline, single} — `src/semantic/mod.rs`
# validates it, and the lowerer's `_ => {}` arm (`src/ir/lowering/mod.rs`) and
# the self-host lowerer's missing `else` (`self_host_lowerer/lower.gg`) are
# unreachable BECAUSE of this rejection. Without it both lowering arms would be
# a Core #10 silent drop of user syntax: a typo'd mode would compile and run
# under the default pool scheduler, which for an async program silently changes
# the interleaving.
#
# The sibling `unknown_directive_error.gg` pins an unknown directive NAME; this
# one pins an unknown directive VALUE, which is a separate arm of the same
# validation and had no fixture.

directive scheduler=bogus

async void main():
    print("unreachable — the directive is rejected at check time")
